1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,080
What do table football, a doll's house and a remote-control car all have in common?
桌上足球、娃娃屋和遥控汽车有什么共同点？

2
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:10,640
They are all smaller versions of real things.
它们都是真实事物的缩小版。

3
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:14,960
And humans have long been intrigued by all things miniature.
而人类长久以来一直对一切微型事物着迷。

4
00:00:14,960 --> 00:00:24,260
The Chinese ancient art of nut carving sees artists sculpt intricate designs, including microscopic people, into fruit or nut stones.
中国古代的核雕艺术中，艺术家们在果核上雕刻精美的图案，包括微小的人物。

5
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:35,880
English author Mary Norton wrote the fictional book series The Borrowers – they are tiny people who live secretly in the walls and floors of a normal-sized house.
英国作家玛丽·诺顿创作了虚构小说系列《借东西的小人》——他们是生活在正常尺寸房屋墙壁和地板缝隙中的微小人物。

6
00:00:35,880 --> 00:00:40,460
And then there are the online channels all about miniature cooking.
此外，还有各种关于微型烹饪的在线频道。

7
00:00:40,460 --> 00:00:54,770
Valarmathi and Rajkumar, who run The Tiny Foods, film tiny versions of traditional Indian dishes being made, set amongst the backdrop of a minuscule village complete with teeny cooking utensils.
经营The Tiny Foods频道的瓦拉玛蒂和拉杰库马尔，拍摄制作传统印度菜肴的微缩版本，背景是一个极小的村庄，配有小小的烹饪器具。

8
00:00:54,770 --> 00:01:03,720
Speaking to the BBC, Valarmathi says she was inspired by her grandmother who 'used to cook in really tiny pots'.
瓦拉玛蒂告诉BBC，她的灵感来自于她的祖母，祖母"过去常常用非常小的锅做饭"。

9
00:01:03,720 --> 00:01:12,540
Similarly, Kate Murdoch, who runs Tiny Kitchen, makes meals cooked on a hob that's powered by a tealight.
同样，经营Tiny Kitchen频道的凯特·默多克，在一个由小蜡烛供能的炉灶上做饭。

10
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:21,610
Her videos include whisking eggs in a tiny mixing bowl and then cooking omelettes in pans the size of a postage stamp.
她的视频包括在一个微小的搅拌碗里搅打鸡蛋，然后在只有邮票大小的平底锅里煎鸡蛋饼。

11
00:01:21,610 --> 00:01:24,580
And then there's the art world…
还有艺术界……

12
00:01:24,580 --> 00:01:30,670
The miniature artist and photographer Tanaka Tatsuya has been rising to online fame.
微型艺术家兼摄影师田中达也在网上逐渐走红。

13
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:36,540
He takes everyday small objects and turns them into new fun-size dioramas.
他利用日常小物件，将它们变成新的趣味尺寸的微缩立体模型。

14
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:48,080
His creations include a face mask resembling lanes in a swimming pool, watermelon mountains and some penguins on an iceberg, which is in fact a bar of soap.
他的作品包括一个类似于游泳池水道的口罩，西瓜山，以及一些在冰山上（实际上是一块肥皂）的企鹅。

15
00:01:48,080 --> 00:01:50,960
So, why do we love small things?
那么，我们为什么喜爱小东西呢？

16
00:01:50,960 --> 00:02:06,550
Simon Garfield, author of In Miniature, says that holding a scaled-down world in our hands, gives us a feeling of control and helps us understand what is too big to envision at full scale, like skyscrapers and railways.
《微缩》一书的作者西蒙·加菲尔德说，将一个按比例缩小的世界捧在手中，给我们一种掌控感，并帮助我们理解那些实物太大而难以想象的事物，比如摩天大楼和铁路。

17
00:02:06,550 --> 00:02:12,160
With models, we can observe, learn and appreciate what we have – with less.
通过模型，我们可以观察、学习并欣赏我们所拥有的——以更小的形式。

18
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:16,280
He discusses how the fascination may also relate to childhood.
他谈到，这种迷恋也可能与童年有关。

19
00:02:16,280 --> 00:02:21,220
Toy dolls and plastic construction kits make us conquerors of worlds.
玩偶和塑料建筑玩具让我们成为世界的征服者。"

20
00:02:21,220 --> 00:02:27,280
'We may never have such dominion over the world again, unless we continue the play into adulthood.'
我们可能再也不会拥有对世界这样的统治权了，除非我们把这种游戏延续到成年。"

21
00:02:27,280 --> 00:02:33,300
So, just like the worlds of art and literature, why not embrace a little love of miniature?
所以，就像艺术和文学世界一样，为什么不欣然接受对微缩事物的一点热爱呢？
